                <pb facs="0794" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg480"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 840.48/278</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-15T20:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 15, 1914, 8 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Your telegram August 15 via Rome relative to German Hamburg-American boats now in
                    New York just received. Will at once take up matter with British and French
                    Governments. Would the German Government be willing to have other German boats
                    here used under the same conditions to carry Americans from other Atlantic ports
                    according to the needs of Americans abroad?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
